{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Build Your Own Mini Framework Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Module Base Class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The abstract interface that every layer implements."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Module:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.training = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise NotImplementedError"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise NotImplementedError"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.training = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def eval(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.training = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Linear Layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The fundamental building block. Stores weights and biases, computes Wx + b forward, and weight/input gradients backward."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Linear(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, fan_in, fan_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        std = math.sqrt(2.0 / fan_in)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.weights = [[random.gauss(0, std) for _ in range(fan_in)] for _ in range(fan_out)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.biases = [0.0] * fan_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.weight_grads = [[0.0] * fan_in for _ in range(fan_out)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bias_grads = [0.0] * fan_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fan_in = fan_in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fan_out = fan_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.input = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.input = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.fan_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            val = self.biases[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(self.fan_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                val += self.weights[i][j] * x[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            output.append(val)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        input_grad = [0.0] * self.fan_in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.fan_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.bias_grads[i] += grad[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(self.fan_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.weight_grads[i][j] += grad[i] * self.input[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                input_grad[j] += grad[i] * self.weights[i][j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return input_grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.fan_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(self.fan_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                params.append((self.weights, i, j, self.weight_grads))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.append((self.biases, i, None, self.bias_grads))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Activation Modules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ReLU, Sigmoid, and Tanh as Modules. Each caches what it needs for the backward pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ReLU(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mask = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mask = [1.0 if v > 0 else 0.0 for v in x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [max(0.0, v) for v in x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [g * m for g, m in zip(grad, self.mask)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Sigmoid(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.output = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.output = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for v in x:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v = max(-500, min(500, v))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.output.append(1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-v)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [g * o * (1 - o) for g, o in zip(grad, self.output)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Tanh(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.output = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.output = [math.tanh(v) for v in x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [g * (1 - o * o) for g, o in zip(grad, self.output)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Dropout Module"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Randomly zeroes elements during training. Scales remaining elements by 1/(1-p) so expected values stay the same. Does nothing during eval."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Dropout(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, p=0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.p = p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mask = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not self.training:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mask = [0.0 if random.random() < self.p else 1.0 / (1 - self.p) for _ in x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [v * m for v, m in zip(x, self.mask)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.mask is None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [g * m for g, m in zip(grad, self.mask)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: BatchNorm Module"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Normalizes activations to zero mean and unit variance per feature across the batch. Maintains running statistics for eval mode."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class BatchNorm(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, size, momentum=0.1, eps=1e-5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.size = size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.gamma = [1.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.beta = [0.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.gamma_grads = [0.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.beta_grads = [0.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.running_mean = [0.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.running_var = [1.0] * size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.momentum = momentum"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.eps = eps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.x_norm = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.std_inv = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.batch_input = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward_batch(self, batch):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        batch_size = len(batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output_batch = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.training:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            mean = [0.0] * self.size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for sample in batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(self.size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    mean[j] += sample[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            mean = [m / batch_size for m in mean]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            var = [0.0] * self.size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for sample in batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(self.size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    var[j] += (sample[j] - mean[j]) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            var = [v / batch_size for v in var]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.std_inv = [1.0 / math.sqrt(v + self.eps) for v in var]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.x_norm = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.batch_input = batch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for sample in batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                normed = [(sample[j] - mean[j]) * self.std_inv[j] for j in range(self.size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.x_norm.append(normed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                output = [self.gamma[j] * normed[j] + self.beta[j] for j in range(self.size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                output_batch.append(output)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(self.size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.running_mean[j] = (1 - self.momentum) * self.running_mean[j] + self.momentum * mean[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.running_var[j] = (1 - self.momentum) * self.running_var[j] + self.momentum * var[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            std_inv = [1.0 / math.sqrt(v + self.eps) for v in self.running_var]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for sample in batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                normed = [(sample[j] - self.running_mean[j]) * std_inv[j] for j in range(self.size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                output = [self.gamma[j] * normed[j] + self.beta[j] for j in range(self.size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                output_batch.append(output)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return output_batch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        result = self.forward_batch([x])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return result[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.x_norm is None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(self.size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.gamma_grads[j] += self.x_norm[0][j] * grad[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.beta_grads[j] += grad[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [grad[j] * self.gamma[j] * self.std_inv[j] for j in range(self.size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(self.size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.append((self.gamma, j, None, self.gamma_grads))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.append((self.beta, j, None, self.beta_grads))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Sequential Container"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Chains modules. Forward goes left-to-right, backward goes right-to-left."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Sequential(Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, *modules):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.modules = list(modules)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for module in self.modules:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = module.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, grad):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for module in reversed(self.modules):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grad = module.backward(grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for module in self.modules:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.extend(module.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.training = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for module in self.modules:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            module.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def eval(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.training = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for module in self.modules:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            module.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Loss Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "MSE and Binary Cross-Entropy. Each returns the loss value and provides a backward() that returns the gradient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class MSELoss:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, predicted, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.predicted = predicted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.target = target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(predicted)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.loss = sum((p - t) ** 2 for p, t in zip(predicted, target)) / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(self.predicted)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [2 * (p - t) / n for p, t in zip(self.predicted, self.target)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class BCELoss:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, predicted, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.predicted = predicted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.target = target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eps = 1e-7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(predicted)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p, t in zip(predicted, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p = max(eps, min(1 - eps, p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.loss += -(t * math.log(p) + (1 - t) * math.log(1 - p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.loss /= n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eps = 1e-7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(self.predicted)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grads = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p, t in zip(self.predicted, self.target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p = max(eps, min(1 - eps, p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grads.append((-t / p + (1 - t) / (1 - p)) / n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 8: SGD and Adam Optimizers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Both take a parameter list and update weights using gradients."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SGD:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, parameters, lr=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.params = parameters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = lr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def step(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for container, i, j, grad_container in self.params:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if j is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                container[i][j] -= self.lr * grad_container[i][j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                container[i] -= self.lr * grad_container[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def zero_grad(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for container, i, j, grad_container in self.params:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if j is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                grad_container[i][j] = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                grad_container[i] = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Adam:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, parameters, lr=0.001, beta1=0.9, beta2=0.999, eps=1e-8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.params = parameters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = lr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.beta1 = beta1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.beta2 = beta2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.eps = eps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.t = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.m = [0.0] * len(parameters)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.v = [0.0] * len(parameters)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def step(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.t += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx, (container, i, j, grad_container) in enumerate(self.params):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if j is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                g = grad_container[i][j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                g = grad_container[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.m[idx] = self.beta1 * self.m[idx] + (1 - self.beta1) * g"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.v[idx] = self.beta2 * self.v[idx] + (1 - self.beta2) * g * g"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            m_hat = self.m[idx] / (1 - self.beta1 ** self.t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v_hat = self.v[idx] / (1 - self.beta2 ** self.t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            update = self.lr * m_hat / (math.sqrt(v_hat) + self.eps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if j is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                container[i][j] -= update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                container[i] -= update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def zero_grad(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for container, i, j, grad_container in self.params:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if j is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                grad_container[i][j] = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                grad_container[i] = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 9: DataLoader"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Splits data into batches, optionally shuffles each epoch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DataLoader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data, batch_size=32, shuffle=True):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.data = data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.batch_size = batch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.shuffle = shuffle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __iter__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indices = list(range(len(self.data)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.shuffle:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            random.shuffle(indices)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for start in range(0, len(indices), self.batch_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            batch_indices = indices[start:start + self.batch_size]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            batch = [self.data[i] for i in batch_indices]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            inputs = [item[0] for item in batch]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            targets = [item[1] for item in batch]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            yield inputs, targets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __len__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return (len(self.data) + self.batch_size - 1) // self.batch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 10: Train a 4-Layer Network on Circle Classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wire everything together. Define a model, pick a loss, pick an optimizer, run the training loop."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_circle_data(n=500, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        label = 1.0 if x * x + y * y < 1.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data.append(([x, y], [label]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Linear(2, 16),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Linear(16, 16),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Linear(16, 8),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Linear(8, 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Sigmoid(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    criterion = BCELoss()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer = Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.01)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = make_circle_data(500)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    split = int(len(data) * 0.8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_data = data[:split]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_data = data[split:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loader = DataLoader(train_data, batch_size=16, shuffle=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_samples = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for batch_inputs, batch_targets in loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            batch_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for x, t in zip(batch_inputs, batch_targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pred = model.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                loss = criterion(pred, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                batch_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                grad = criterion.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                model.backward(grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                predicted_class = 1.0 if pred[0] >= 0.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if predicted_class == t[0]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    total_correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total_samples += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_loss += batch_loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_loss = total_loss / total_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accuracy = total_correct / total_samples * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if epoch % 10 == 0 or epoch == 99:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"Epoch {epoch:3d} | Loss: {avg_loss:.6f} | Train Accuracy: {accuracy:.1f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for x, t in test_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = model.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        predicted_class = 1.0 if pred[0] >= 0.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if predicted_class == t[0]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_accuracy = correct / len(test_data) * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\nTest Accuracy: {test_accuracy:.1f}% ({correct}/{len(test_data)})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model, test_accuracy"
      ]
    },
